From 57b63dde7d1e0aa1585bf25252b3d007938e0c2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AtlasOS <atlasos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:37:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] AtlasOS look for the first-run wizard

- Buttons as in Atlas.Ui 1.4 (4 px corners, 6 px pressed; the step forward
  in the accent colour), step dots, a big
  bold title and a rounder card with a shadow, as in the Atlas apps
- Welcome screen: the AtlasOS logo, "Welcome to AtlasOS" and one accent
  button; credit Fedora and KDE Plasma underneath
- Appearance page: AtlasOS Light or Dark as two pictures of the desktop,
  applying AtlasOS's Global Themes (Fedora's patch named themes AtlasOS
  removes, so choosing Dark did nothing)
- Rounded sections behind the lists, the AtlasOS logo on the last page
- The welcome wallpaper falls back to the light picture when there is no
  dark one (a url that wasn't found is still truthy)
- Components for AtlasOS's own setup pages: AtlasButton, ChoiceCard,
  DesktopPreview, SectionBackground
- Language, keyboard and Wi-Fi pages skip themselves when Atlas Installer
  already asked: /etc/atlasos/installer.ini has the language or keyboard
  layout, or a network that came along and is fully online now
- Choosing a theme no longer freezes the wizard: the theme applies in the
  background and the old look fades into the new one (about 400 ms; none
  under reduced motion); the choice card's ring animates too
